	skos:definition "An activity performed by a road user."@en , "Behaviour tag."@en ;
	skos:editorialNote "Conditional rules (boolean+value co-occurrence) are ontology integrity constraints motivated by ISO 34503:2023, 12.4 (conditional attribute dependencies in ODD specifications)."@en , "v1 had no normative reference; was attributed solely to ASAM OpenLABEL. ISO 34504 Section 4.4.4 defines the same action taxonomy (accelerating, decelerating, lane change, etc.) as tags for dynamic entities. ISO 34501 Term 2.15 formally defines 'action/activity' as 'single purposeful act or behaviour executed by any actor'."@en ;
	skos:exactMatch openlabel_tagging:Behaviour ;
	skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/ascs-ev/envited-x/openlabel/v1.1.0-alpha> ;
	skos:note "ISO 34504:2023, 4.4.4 (Tags for a dynamic entity — longitudinal, lateral, and mixed actions); ISO 34501:2022, Term 2.15 (action/activity)"@en .
openlabel_tagging:BehaviourCommunication a owl:ObjectProperty ;
	rdfs:label "BehaviourCommunication"@en ;
	rdfs:range openlabel_tagging:BehaviourCommunicationEnum ;
	skos:definition "Communication type of road user behaviour."@en ;
	skos:editorialNote "Communication signals (horn, headlight flash, indicators) are not explicitly covered by ISO 34504 action tags. Retained from ASAM OpenLABEL as scenario-relevant communication modality."@en ;
	skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/ascs-ev/envited-x/openlabel/v1.1.0-alpha> ;
	skos:note "ASAM OpenLABEL V1.0.0"@en .
